{
 "_about": "Genealogies isnady draws (GEN1). Each node: id, parent, names (en, tr, ar), kind (prophet, caliph, imam, person); gap: generations between it and its parent are not known or left out; disputed: the reports differ (with a note). Written for isnady from the Sunni sources, in this order of strength: (1) the Qur'an where it names a relation; (2) al-Bukhari, Sahih, Kitab Manaqib al-Ansar, Bab Mab'ath al-Nabi: the Prophet's lineage up to 'Adnan; (3) the sira and history works: Ibn Hisham, al-Sira al-Nabawiyya; Ibn Sa'd, al-Tabaqat al-Kubra; al-Tabari, Tarikh al-Rusul wa-l-Muluk; Ibn Kathir, Qisas al-Anbiya' and al-Bidaya wa-l-Nihaya; (4) the genealogists: Mus'ab al-Zubayri, Nasab Quraysh; Ibn Hazm, Jamharat Ansab al-'Arab. The names between Adam and Ibrahim and between Isma'il and 'Adnan come only from (3), who took them partly from the People of the Book. Not yet checked node by node against printed pages (TODO GEN1-K).",
